 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>The <b>Color</b> class (in <code>java.awt</code>) represents colors using <b>RGB</b> values (Red, Green, Blue), each from 0 to 255.</p><h3>Key points</h3><ul><li>Make a color: <code>new Color(r, g, b)</code>.</li><li>Use constants: <code>Color.RED</code>, <code>Color.BLUE</code>, etc.</li><li>Set drawing color: <code>g2.setPaint(c)</code> or <code>g.setColor(c)</code>, then draw/fill.</li><li>Component colors: <code>setBackground(c)</code>, <code>setForeground(c)</code>.</li><li><code>brighter()</code> and <code>darker()</code> give lighter/darker shades.</li></ul>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "new Color(0, 0, 255) gives which color?",
  "options": [
   "Red",
   "Green",
   "Blue"
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "why": "R, G, B: third value is Blue."
 }
